  "week_ahead": {
    "text": "The dollar dominates amid slew of US data and Mideast tensions , with US data in focus this week . USD/JPY is knocking on the door of a major breakout, but BOJ intervention risk continues to keep traders on edge as the deterioration of the former ceasefire between the USA and Iran continues into daily exchanges of fire centred around the Strait of Hormuz, with the Strait effectively closed to shipping . BOJ's interest rate decision will determine whether USD/JPY can extend higher , presenting the critical pivot for the week. Watch USD/JPY closely as it balances Fed tightening expectations against potential BOJ intervention and geopolitical risk premium. If the Strait closure does not change quickly, the price of crude oil is going to trade higher when markets open this week , adding inflationary pressure that could derail rate cut bets.",
